 "prompt": "A footage-pack edit: the user drops a pile of loose travel and event clips of assorted lengths — throwaway takes included — and asks for the highlights cut into a reel, with the blurry, repetitive and boring parts thrown out. Here: 12 clips cut from CC-licensed contemporary footage (aerial beaches, Japanese coastline, Sikkim mountains, a mountain stream, a train window), deliberately salted with one out-of-focus take, two near-duplicates and a 22-second static stretch. The system described all 12, analysed all 12, and cut 57 seconds from eight of them — eight different sources against the asked-for ~60 — leaving out every salted throwaway. The pack is silent, so there is no speech to subtitle: the short on-screen lines are authored per selected clip and burned over that clip's window. The vertical phone clip letterboxes into the 1080p frame rather than being stretched. No score — the brief asks for a music-synced cut and the music backend is currently unavailable.",
